 and note crossover endorsements for Ossoff"], "rationale": "Polling since midsummer is unusually consistent, with even Trafalgar, Rasmussen and InsiderAdvantage showing Ossoff ahead, and aggregates cluster near seven to eight points. Combined with a roughly 20-to-1 cash advantage, markets in the mid-nineties, and ratings centered on Likely D, the evidence supports a clear but not unassailable Democratic lead.", "watch": "A strong Collins debate performance or a late shift in the national midterm environment toward Republicans could compress the polling gap.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Jon Ossoff enters the final weeks of his reelection bid as a clear favorite in a state with only a slight Republican tilt. Polling has been remarkably steady: every pollster surveyed, including those with Republican-leaning sponsors such as Trafalgar, Rasmussen and InsiderAdvantage, shows Ossoff leading Mike Collins, with recent margins ranging from four to eleven points and aggregates settling around seven to eight. Expert ratings cluster at Likely D, and prediction markets place his win probability in the mid-nineties.\n\nResources reinforce that picture. Ossoff has raised more than $77 million and holds over $42 million on hand, while Collins has about $2 million, and outside groups have spent more opposing the Republican than supporting him. News reports describe Republican hopes in Georgia fading, and Ossoff has drawn crossover support, including a GOP agriculture official's endorsement. Remaining questions concern the final margin rather than the likely winner, though debates and turnout always carry some risk.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "